# FA3 SM90 Forward: Continuous K/V Pipeline Across Work-Tiles

This is the mechanism FA3 uses to avoid a per-tile K/V pipeline-fill bubble. The crux is **#2 and #3**: K/V `PipelineState` lives outside the work-tile loop and never resets; the producer keeps issuing into the same 2-stage ring across tiles, throttled only by empty-barrier backpressure—not by waiting for the consumer to fully drain tile N.

---

## 1. Persistent loop: producer vs consumer structure

Both warpgroups share one CTA and run separate persistent loops. The **producer (warp group 0)** calls `mainloop.load()` once per valid work-tile; **consumers (MMA warp groups 1–2)** call `mainloop.mma()` then `epilogue.store()`.

**Producer** — `PipelineState` and loop declared outside the loop; `load()` called inside:

```320:374:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_fwd_kernel_sm90.h
        if (warp_group_idx == 0) {  // Producer
            cutlass::arch::warpgroup_reg_dealloc<LoadRegisterRequirement>();
            // ...
            PipelineState smem_pipe_write = cutlass::make_producer_start_state<MainloopPipelineK>();
            PipelineState smem_pipe_write_new = cutlass::make_producer_start_state<MainloopPipelineKVNew>();
            int work_idx = 0;
            // ...
            for (auto work_tile_info = SingleProducerWarp || warp_idx_in_warpgroup == 0 ? scheduler.template get_initial_work</*IsProducerWarp=*/true>(params.scheduler) : scheduler.template get_initial_work</*IsProducerWarp=*/false>(params.scheduler);
                 work_tile_info.is_valid(params.scheduler);
                 work_tile_info = SingleProducerWarp || warp_idx_in_warpgroup == 0 ? scheduler.template get_next_work</*IsProducerWarp=*/true>(params.scheduler, work_tile_info) : scheduler.template get_next_work</*IsProducerWarp=*/false>(params.scheduler, work_tile_info)) {
                // ...
                mainloop.load(params.mainloop, pipeline_k, pipeline_v, pipeline_vt, smem_pipe_write,
                                         shared_storage, scheduler_prefetch, seqlen_info, block_coord, work_idx);
            }
            mainloop.load_tail(pipeline_k, pipeline_v, pipeline_vt, smem_pipe_write, shared_storage, work_idx);
```

**Consumer** — separate loop; `get_next_work` is called **after `mma()` but before epilogue** (not in the `for` increment):

```375:468:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_fwd_kernel_sm90.h
        } else {  // Consumer
            cutlass::arch::warpgroup_reg_alloc<MmaRegisterRequirement>();
            // ...
            PipelineState smem_pipe_read;
            PipelineState smem_pipe_read_new;
            // ...
            scheduler.init_consumer();
            mainloop.mma_init();
            int work_idx = 0;
            CUTLASS_PRAGMA_NO_UNROLL
            for (auto work_tile_info = scheduler.template get_initial_work</*IsProducerWarp=*/false>(params.scheduler);
                 work_tile_info.is_valid(params.scheduler);
                 ) {
                // ...
                tile_valid = mainloop.mma(/*...*/, smem_pipe_read, /*...*/);
                // Do this here before the epilogue so that the next tile is ready to go.
                work_tile_info = scheduler.template get_next_work</*IsProducerWarp=*/false>(params.scheduler, work_tile_info);
                // ...
                if (tile_valid) {
                    epilogue.store(/*...*/);
                } else {
                    epilogue.store_zero(/*...*/);
                }
            }
```

**Answer:** Yes, producer calls `mainloop.load()` exactly once per work-tile inside the persistent loop. Producer and consumer are **not** structurally identical (consumer splits tile advance from epilogue), but they process the same tile sequence via the scheduler.

---

## 2. Pipeline state persistence (THE CRUX)

### Declaration relative to the work-tile loop

| Role | Variable | Where declared | Initialized |
|------|----------|----------------|-------------|
| Producer | `smem_pipe_write` | **Before** persistent `for` | Once: `make_producer_start_state<MainloopPipelineK>()` |
| Consumer | `smem_pipe_read` | **Before** persistent `for` | Default ctor `{index=0, phase=0, count=0}` |

Producer (lines 327–328, 340–372 above). Consumer (lines 381–382, 391–394 above).

### Never reset per tile

Inside `load()` and `mma()`, the state is passed by reference and advanced with `++smem_pipe_write` / `++smem_pipe_read`. There is **no** reassignment to `make_producer_start_state` at tile boundaries.

At the end of each `load()`:

```921:928:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
        scheduler_prefetch();
        // ...
        if constexpr (Transpose_V) { copy_Vt_to_V(smem_pipe_write); }
        ++smem_pipe_write;
        // At the end, all threads have the correct smem_pipe_write.
        ++work_idx;
```

At the end of each `mma()` (IntraWGOverlap path):

```1337:1341:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
            warpgroup_wait<0>();
            pipeline_v.consumer_release(smem_pipe_read);  // release V, otherwise producers will hang
            softmax.rescale_o(tOrO, scores_scale);
            // ...
            ++smem_pipe_read;
```

### Phase/index semantics

`PipelineState` is a circular `(index, phase, count)` counter:

```170:213:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/csrc/cutlass/include/cutlass/pipeline/sm90_pipeline.hpp
struct PipelineState {
  static constexpr uint32_t Stages = Stages_;
  int index_ = 0;
  uint32_t phase_ = 0;
  uint32_t count_ = 0;
  // ...
  void operator++() {
    if constexpr (Stages > 0) {
      ++index_;
      ++count_;
      if (index_ == Stages) {
        index_ = 0;
        phase_ ^= 1;
      }
    }
  }
```

Producer start state (phase inverted because buffers start empty):

```252:260:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/csrc/cutlass/include/cutlass/pipeline/sm90_pipeline.hpp
PipelineState<Pipeline::Stages> make_producer_start_state() {
  constexpr int InitialProducerStage = 0;
  constexpr uint32_t InitialProducerPhase = 1;
  constexpr uint32_t InitialProducerCount = 0;
  return {InitialProducerStage, InitialProducerPhase, InitialProducerCount};
}
```

**Answer:** Full/empty mbarrier **phases continue across work-tiles**. The 2-stage K/V ring is one global stream for the CTA lifetime; tile N+1's first `load_K` uses the same carried-over `(index, phase)` as where tile N's `load()` left off. Barriers are initialized once at kernel entry (lines 245–284 in `flash_fwd_kernel_sm90.h`), not per tile.

---

## 3. Producer K/V load loop, backpressure, and cross-tile overlap

### Backpressure: `producer_acquire` waits on empty (consumer-released) barrier

```787:797:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
        auto load_K = [&] (int const n_block, auto const& smem_pipe_write, auto need_seqlenk_masking_type) {
            pipeline_k.producer_acquire(smem_pipe_write);
            if constexpr (!PagedKVNonTMA) {
                // TMA K into smem_pipe_write.index()
                copy(params.tma_load_K.with(*pipeline_k.producer_get_barrier(smem_pipe_write), /*...*/),
                    tKgK_TMA(_, n_block_idx, bidb_kv_idx), tKsK_TMA(_, smem_pipe_write.index()));
            } else {
                paged_kv_manager.template load_K<Seqlenk_mask>(n_block, sK_pi(_, _, smem_pipe_write.index()));
                pipeline_k.producer_commit(smem_pipe_write, cutlass::arch::cpasync_barrier_arrive);
            }
        };
```

CUTLASS implementation:

```501:509:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/csrc/cutlass/include/cutlass/pipeline/sm90_pipeline.hpp
  void producer_acquire(uint32_t stage, uint32_t phase, ProducerToken barrier_token) {
    // ...
    if (barrier_token != BarrierStatus::WaitDone) {
      empty_barrier_ptr_[stage].wait(phase);  // BACKPRESSURE: wait for consumer release
    }
    if (params_.is_leader) {
      full_barrier_ptr_[stage].arrive_and_expect_tx(params_.transaction_bytes);
    }
  }
```

Consumer releases a stage after MMA consumes it:

```1259:1259:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
                pipeline_k.consumer_release(smem_pipe_read);  // release K
```

(FA3's `PipelineTmaAsyncNoCluster` has only warp-group-leader signal on `consumer_release`.)

### Inner n_block loop (within one work-tile)

```898:920:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
        #pragma unroll (!Transpose_V && Use_TMA_KV ? 2 : 1)
        for (; n_block >= n_block_min; --n_block) {
            PipelineState smem_pipe_write_v = smem_pipe_write; // copy the state, write_v is always 1 step behind
            ++smem_pipe_write;
            if (should_load_KV) {
                // ...
                load_K(n_block, smem_pipe_write, cute::false_type{} /*Seqlenk_mask*/);
                if constexpr (!Transpose_V) {
                    if constexpr (IntraWGOverlap) {
                        load_V(n_block_prev, smem_pipe_write_v, cute::true_type{} /*Seqlenk_mask*/);
                    } else {
                        load_V(n_block, smem_pipe_write, cute::false_type{} /*Seqlenk_mask*/);
                    }
                }
            }
            n_block_prev = n_block;
            if constexpr (Transpose_V) { copy_Vt_to_V(smem_pipe_write_v); }
        }
```

Each K/V issue: `++smem_pipe_write` then `producer_acquire` → TMA → (TMA completion commits via barrier embedded in TMA descriptor).

### Cross-tile: tile N+1 K/V starts before consumer drains tile N

**Critical ordering at the start of each `load()` call** (including tile N+1):

```838:891:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
        if (should_load_KV) {
            // ...
            if constexpr (Transpose_V) { load_V(n_block, smem_pipe_write, /*...*/); }
            load_K(n_block, smem_pipe_write, cute::true_type{} /*Seqlenk_mask*/);  // <-- FIRST: K for new tile
        }

        if constexpr (Use_TMA_Q) {
            // Wait for the MMA warpgroups to signal that smem_q is ready
            cutlass::arch::NamedBarrier::sync(/*...*/, FwdNamedBarriers::QueryEmpty);
            // THEN: TMA Q
        }
        // ...
        shared_storage.pipelines.barrier_O.wait((work_idx + 1) % 2);
        // THEN: rest of K/V loop
```

**Answer:** `load()` for work-tile N+1 **does** begin issuing K (and optionally V) into the carried-over ring **before** waiting on `QueryEmpty` or for tile N's consumer to finish. It does **not** wait for tile N's consumer to fully drain. Throttling is only:

1. `producer_acquire` → `empty_barrier[stage].wait(phase)` if that ring slot is still held by the consumer from tile N's trailing n_blocks.
2. Later: `QueryEmpty` (Q reuse) and `barrier_O` (smem aliasing with epilogue O).

If the consumer is slow, the producer stalls on (1)—not on an explicit per-tile fence. If the consumer is fast enough, tile N+1's first K TMAs overlap with tile N's trailing MMA/epilogue → **no inter-tile pipeline bubble**.

---

## 4. Q buffering (single smem buffer, ping-pong barriers)

### Smem: one Q buffer (not multi-stage)

```130:132:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
    using SmemLayoutAtomQ = decltype(cutlass::gemm::collective::detail::ss_smem_selector<GMMA::Major::K, Element,
        decltype(cute::get<0>(TileShape_MNK{})), decltype(cute::get<2>(TileShape_MNK{}))>());
    using SmemLayoutQ = decltype(tile_to_shape(SmemLayoutAtomQ{}, select<0, 2>(TileShape_MNK{})));
```

No `Int<kStages>` on Q—**single-buffered in smem**. K/V have `Int<kStages>{}` in their layouts (line 138).

Q pipeline barriers (separate from K/V TMA pipeline):

```109:114:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_fwd_kernel_sm90.h
        struct PipelineStorage : cute::aligned_struct<16, _1> {
            alignas(16) BarrierQ barrier_Q;
            alignas(16) BarrierQ barrier_Qv;
            alignas(16) cutlass::arch::ClusterBarrier barrier_O;
            alignas(16) typename CollectiveMainloop::MainloopPipelineK::SharedStorage pipeline_k;
            alignas(16) typename CollectiveMainloop::MainloopPipelineV::SharedStorage pipeline_v;
```

### Ping-pong protocol (work_idx phase)

**Consumer** waits on Q before MMA; signals Q free after MMA:

```1168:1170:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
        auto &barrier_Q = shared_storage.pipelines.barrier_Q;
        if constexpr (!AppendKV) {
            barrier_Q.wait(work_idx % 2);
```

```1324:1325:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
            // Tell producers that smem_q is ready
            cutlass::arch::NamedBarrier::arrive(/*...*/, FwdNamedBarriers::QueryEmpty);
```

**Producer** waits on `QueryEmpty`, then loads Q, then waits on `barrier_O`:

```850:858:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
        if constexpr (Use_TMA_Q) {
            cutlass::arch::NamedBarrier::sync(/*...*/, FwdNamedBarriers::QueryEmpty);
            if ((SingleProducerWarp || warp_idx_in_warpgroup == 0) && cute::elect_one_sync()) {
                shared_storage.pipelines.barrier_Q.arrive_and_expect_tx(TmaTransactionBytesQ);
                copy(params.tma_load_Q.with(/* barrier_Q */, /*...*/), tQgQ, tQsQ);
```

**Bootstrapping:** `mma_init()` arrives on `QueryEmpty` so the first producer `load()` can proceed:

```971:977:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
    mma_init() {
        // Tell producers that smem_q is ready
        cutlass::arch::NamedBarrier::arrive(/*...*/, FwdNamedBarriers::QueryEmpty);
```

### PackGQA path (vLLM default)

For PackGQA with `kBlockH==1`: `Use_TMA_Q = false` → Q loaded via `cp.async` (`PackGQAManager::load_Q`), same `QueryEmpty` + `barrier_Q` protocol (lines 866–874).

For PackGQA with `kBlockH>1` (GQA ratio 4/8/16): TMA Q is enabled via `PackGQA_TMA`.

### Why `barrier_O`?

`smem_o` (epilogue) **aliases `smem_v`** in a union:

```98:107:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_fwd_kernel_sm90.h
    struct SharedStorage {
        struct TensorStorage : cute::aligned_struct<128, _1> {
            union {
                struct {
                    // ...
                    typename CollectiveMainloop::TensorStorage mainloop;
                };
                // We want smem_o to line up with the start of smem_v
                typename CollectiveEpilogue::TensorStorage epilogue;
            };
        } tensors;
```

Producer waits `barrier_O.wait((work_idx + 1) % 2)` after Q load so epilogue O-writes to `smem_v`/`smem_o` from tile N complete before producer reuses that smem for V TMA on tile N+1. Epilogue signals via `barrier_O.arrive()` after O is written (e.g. `epilogue_fwd.hpp:353`).

**Answer:** Q is **not** ring-buffered like K/V. It uses **one smem buffer + 2-phase ping-pong** on `barrier_Q` (`work_idx % 2`) and `QueryEmpty` named barrier. Producer can prefetch tile N+1 K into the ring while consumer still reads tile N's Q; producer cannot overwrite Q until consumer arrives on `QueryEmpty`.

---

## 5. hd128 bf16 causal: stages, tiles, smem

### Tile sizes and kStages

From `tile_size.h` for headdim ≤ 128, non-`use_one_mma_wg`:

```40:45:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/tile_size.h
        } else if (headdim <= 128) {
            if (use_one_mma_wg) {
                return {64, is_causal || is_local || paged_kv_non_TMA ? 128 : 176, true, true};
            } else {
                return {128, is_causal || is_local || paged_kv_non_TMA ? 128 : 160, true, true};
            }
```

For **hd128 bf16 causal** (standard 2-MMA-WG path):

| Parameter | Value |
|-----------|-------|
| `kBlockM` | **128** |
| `kBlockN` | **128** |
| `MmaPV_is_RS` | **true** (P in registers) |
| `IntraWGOverlap` | **true** |
| `kStages` | **2** (hardcoded for SM90) |

```48:48:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_fwd_launch_template.h
    static constexpr int kStages = Arch >= 90 ? 2 : std::get<3>(kBlockMN_kNWarps_Stages_RS);
```

### SharedStorage layout

Mainloop tensor storage (no transpose-V, RS PV → `TensorStorageWithoutPNoTranspose`):

```319:325:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
    struct TensorStorageWithoutPNoTranspose : cute::aligned_struct<...> {
        cute::array_aligned<Element, cute::cosize_v<SmemLayoutVt>, ...> smem_v;   // kStages deep
        cute::array_aligned<Element, cute::cosize_v<SmemLayoutQ>, ...> smem_q;     // single buffer
        cute::array_aligned<Element, cute::cosize_v<SmemLayoutK>, ...> smem_k;     // kStages deep
        SmemQv_t smem_qv;
        cute::array_aligned<ElementSAux, cute::cosize_v<SmemLayoutSAux>, 128> smem_s_aux;
    };
```

**Union:** mainloop tensor storage is in a **union with epilogue** so `smem_o` overlays `smem_v` (kernel lines 98–107 above). Q is **not** in that union; only epilogue O overlaps V.

### Approximate smem bytes (hd128, bf16, kBlockM=N=128, kStages=2)

| Buffer | Size (bytes) |
|--------|-------------|
| `smem_q` | 128×128×2 = **32,768** |
| `smem_k` | 128×128×2×2 = **65,536** |
| `smem_v` | 128×128×2×2 = **65,536** |
| `smem_s_aux` | 64×2 = **128** |
| Mainloop data subtotal | **~164 KB** |
| `smem_o` (epilogue) | 128×128×2 = **32,768** (aliases `smem_v` base) |
| Pipeline mbarriers (`pipeline_k`, `pipeline_v`, `barrier_Q/O`, scheduler smem) | small fixed overhead |

Total `SharedStorageSize = sizeof(SharedStorage)` is a compile-time constant; launch sets dynamic smem if ≥ 48 KB (`flash_fwd_launch_template.h:182–191`). Comments elsewhere reference ~227 KB for heavier configs; hd128 128×128 RS is toward the **~160–170 KB** range for mainloop tensors plus barriers.

---

## 6. Scheduler: same tile sequence, lockstep agreement

### Which scheduler (vLLM path: varlen + causal)

```65:78:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_fwd_launch_template.h
    using SchedulerPersistent = std::conditional_t<Varlen,
        flash::VarlenDynamicPersistentTileScheduler<kBlockM, kBlockN, /*...*/, LPT, Sort, true /*Prepared*/>,
        std::conditional_t<!Is_causal && !Is_local,
            flash::StaticPersistentTileScheduler<Split>,
            flash::DynamicPersistentTileScheduler</*...*/>
        >
    >;
    static constexpr bool UsePersistentScheduler = Arch >= 90 ? !(Split && !Varlen) : /*...*/;
```

vLLM uses **varlen + packgqa + causal** → `VarlenDynamicPersistentTileScheduler` with **LPT** (longest-processing-time-first: `block = num_m_blocks - 1 - block` at line 610 in `tile_scheduler.hpp`).

### Same sequence, not same progress

Both warpgroups iterate the **same logical tile sequence**, but the producer can run **ahead** on K/V loads. Agreement mechanism:

1. **Initial tile:** both start from `blockIdx.x` (persistent grid = `#SMs`).
2. **Next tile prefetch** (during `load()`, before tile finishes):

```657:662:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/tile_scheduler.hpp
    prefetch_next_work(Params const& params, WorkTileInfo& current_work) const {
        if (threadIdx.x % NumProducerThreads == 0) {
            current_work.tile_idx = atomicAdd(params.tile_count_semaphore, 1) + int(gridDim.x);
        }
    }
```

Called from producer at end of `load()` via `scheduler_prefetch` lambda (kernel line 367–369).

3. **Broadcast next tile** via named barriers + smem (`StreamkBarrier0/1`):

```665:685:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/tile_scheduler.hpp
    get_next_work(Params const& params, WorkTileInfo const& current_work) const {
        if constexpr (IsProducerWarp) {
            int new_tile_idx = __shfl_sync(0xffffffff, current_work.tile_idx, 0);
            WorkTileInfo work_info = tile_idx_to_work_tile(params, new_tile_idx, /*...*/);
            flash::named_barrier_sync(NumThreads, StreamkBarrier0);  // TileCountSmemEmpty
            if (threadIdx.x % cutlass::NumThreadsPerWarp == 0) {
                *work_info_smem = make_int4(work_info.tile_idx, work_info.block, work_info.bidh, work_info.bidb);
            }
            flash::named_barrier_arrive(NumThreads, StreamkBarrier1);  // TileCountSmemFull
            return work_info;
        } else {
            flash::named_barrier_sync(NumThreads, StreamkBarrier1);  // TileCountSmemFull
            int4 work_info = *work_info_smem;
            flash::named_barrier_arrive(NumThreads, StreamkBarrier0);
            return WorkTileInfo{work_info.x, work_info.y, work_info.z, work_info.w};
        }
    }
```

Consumers call `init_consumer()` / arrive on `StreamkBarrier0` at startup (kernel lines 335, 386; scheduler lines 328–334).

**Answer:** Producer and consumer stay on the **same work-tile sequence** via atomic global scheduling + named-barrier broadcast of `(tile_idx, block, bidh, bidb)`. They are **not** lockstep on processing phase—producer may be loading tile N+1 K/V while consumer is still in tile N MMA/epilogue. The **K/V ring** is the cross-tile continuity mechanism; the **scheduler barriers** only synchronize *which* tile is next.

---

## Mechanism summary (avoiding inter-tile bubble)

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  subgraph Producer["Producer WG (persistent)"]
    PSW["smem_pipe_write<br/>(outside loop, never reset)"]
    LK["load_K/V → ring[stage]<br/>producer_acquire(empty)"]
    LQ["load Q after QueryEmpty"]
    PSW --> LK --> LQ
  end
  subgraph Ring["K/V smem ring (kStages=2)"]
    S0["stage 0"]
    S1["stage 1"]
  end
  subgraph Consumer["Consumer WGs (persistent)"]
    PSR["smem_pipe_read<br/>(outside loop, never reset)"]
    MMA["mma: consumer_wait(full)<br/>consumer_release(empty)"]
    PSR --> MMA
  end
  LK --> Ring
  Ring --> MMA
  MMA -->|"empty barrier"| LK
```

1. **One global K/V ring per CTA** — `PipelineState` declared before the work-tile loop; phases/index never reset per tile.
2. **Tile N+1 K prefetch overlaps tile N consumer** — first `load_K` of the next `load()` runs before Q sync; backpressure is only `empty_barrier.wait(phase)` per stage.
3. **Q is separate** — single smem buffer, ping-pong via `barrier_Q[work_idx%2]` + `QueryEmpty`; does not participate in the K/V ring.
4. **smem_v / smem_o alias** — `barrier_O[(work_idx+1)%2]` prevents V TMA from colliding with epilogue O writes.
5. **Scheduler** — atomic work stealing + named-barrier tile broadcast keeps producer/consumer on the same tile IDs while allowing K/V pipeline to run ahead across tile boundaries.

For your port: the essential invariant is **do not re-initialize or drain the K/V pipeline at work-tile boundaries**—only advance `PipelineState` continuously and rely on stage empty barriers for backpressure. Q and O need their own ping-pong barriers because they use single smem slots (with O aliasing V).

